{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Investigation (read-only, box i-00880b2c7f13527c5, 2026-11-22). All times PST.\n\n### Observation\n- Review-bot journal, 11-20 18:33 to 11-22 08:30: 12 containers. In every one, the first 1-2 reviews that need a new snapshot log `merge_detection`, then nothing (no LLM keepalive, no git output) until the 1200 s timeout.\n- The abandoned review threads in each container all fail at the same second, with `git read-tree <sha> failed: cannot change to gate-scratch/reviewbot-...: No such file`. That moment is a fixed time after the container started: 45.3, 44.8, 45.3, 45.8 min (11-20 containers 5879, e50c, 0e3c, 269e); 47.3, 48.5, 48.6, 49.3, 49.5, 49.5 min (11-21 containers 39b8, 95f1, 94a6, 7d59, 9dc7, e43a); 50.7, 51.5 min (11-21 22:17 b73e, 11-22 02:59 e08c). Reviews after that point take the normal 2-7 min.\n- I53d60ec: container 95f1 started 05:54:48; review began 05:55:50 and timed out 06:15:50; its thread and I8be210f's both failed at 06:43:21 (48.5 min after start).\n- Timeout counts per PST day (journal `VOTER_ERROR ... review timed out`): 11-17 0, 11-18 0, 11-19 0, 11-20 5, 11-21 6.\n- 384e0af92d1 \"Order snapshot link changes against byte totals\" merged 11-20 12:28 PST. It moved `janitor.startup_sweep`'s full-store walk (`cache.distinct_bytes` over every entry) inside the store-wide `accounting_lock` (`locks/bytes.total.lock`). The review-bot starts that sweep on a thread at every container start (`app.lifespan` -> `start_background_janitor`). Every snapshot build takes the same lock to publish (`_build_publish_account`), with a blocking flock and no timeout.\n- Snapshot store on the box: 316 `tickets-<sha>` entries of about 224,000 files each, 192 code entries, 4.49M inodes on the gate-scratch volume. `find` over one tickets entry took 7.4 s, so one walk is roughly 39 min of directory traversal before Python's per-file `lstat`.\n- Scratch-folder errors: 17 distinct `reviewbot-*` folders referenced on 11-21. All 17 belong to a review that started in the same container and was abandoned on timeout. The cancelled coroutine's `TemporaryDirectory` removed the folder while its worker thread was still blocked on the lock. None refers to a previous container's folder.\n- `write lock still held` (tickets store) and `git maintenance ... timed out after 120s` lines occur in every container, including periods with no stall, and do not line up with the stall windows.\n\n### Hypotheses\n1. The startup sweep holds the accounting lock for about 45-51 minutes, and every review that must build a new snapshot waits on it silently. The wait is before the LLM call and has no bound or log line.\n2. Tickets-store write-lock contention stalls reviews.\n3. Clone or snapshot I/O blocked behind git maintenance stalls reviews.\n\n### Experiment\n- Local reproduction (`.rebar/scratch/05f74084-nettlefish/repro/repro_sweep_blocks.py`, run from a checkout at 39d78c81fd5): inject a 15 s delay into the sweep's walk, start `startup_sweep` on a thread, then build a ticket snapshot for a new SHA. Result: the build waited 15.0 s and emitted no log line with DEBUG logging on. This supports hypothesis 1.\n- Hypotheses 2 and 3 are not supported: the stall end-point tracks container start time to within 7 min across 12 containers, while the write-lock and maintenance lines have no such alignment. The write-lock lines are the artifact-emit write after a vote, which happens after the LLM call, not before it.\n\n### Root cause\nThe janitor's startup sweep holds `accounting_lock` for the full-store walk (about 50 minutes on this store), and the snapshot build in every review waits on that lock with no timeout and no log line. Each autodeploy recreates the container and restarts the sweep, so each deploy brings another stall window, which keeps the bot busy and spends the deferral bound."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795383935846160001,"uuid":"8e60ebab-02ca-42bf-8018-889c3a39c972"}